      "findings": "## Findings\n\nnone\n\n## Blockers\n\n- In [the profile](memory-profile.md#comparison-rationale), `representational_form` asserts `known` coverage while its unit \u201cWorkspace executable bindings; task histories; manifest predictions; cache/trace access structures and summary metadata\u201d classifies normalized JSON as symbolic without separately accounting for the retained message content consumed by the debugger. [EPI-RTE-trace-normalization](epistemic.md#epi-rte-trace-normalization) identifies an evidence projection from cached messages to a natural-language diagnosis consumer; [RT-RTE-auxiliary-analysis](runtime.md#rt-rte-auxiliary-analysis) identifies the selected trace evidence delivered to that model. JSON structure is not the form of every operative payload. The included saved-output and full-trace/history checkpoints likewise have only a fixed-code serialization/projection warrant in [RT-RTE-context-control](runtime.md#rt-rte-context-control), not a complete classification of every consumed body. In addition, the unit \u201cDriver and portable rationale/evidence fields, separate from prediction and status fields\u201d nevertheless contains both prose and symbolic prediction/status findings with different consumers, contrary to the required operative-part/consumption-path split; [EPI-OBJ-manifest-rationale](epistemic.md#epi-obj-manifest-rationale), [EPI-OBJ-manifest-predictions](epistemic.md#epi-obj-manifest-predictions) and [MEM-OBJ-portable-manifests](memory.md#mem-obj-portable-manifests) preserve those distinctions. Comparison consumers would incorrectly infer a completely classified form inventory and resolved mixed-payload units. Split the materially different parts/consumption paths and retain uncertainty wherever accepted records do not resolve payload form. A synthesis caveat cannot preserve an extracted `known` assessment; the defect must be repaired in the profile itself. The supported existence of natural-language and symbolic memory remains intact.\n\n## Limits\n\n- The partial behavioral-authority inventory omits the learning effect of retained session/tool messages at the emergency-summary update consumer. [MEM-OBJ-emergency-summary](memory.md#mem-obj-emergency-summary) establishes that those messages feed automatic production of retained continuation guidance received by the retry; the profile itself recognizes this route under trace learning but its authority unit covers only the output's downstream knowledge and instruction effects. The emitted learning finding remains supported by the separate harness-update route, and the authority axis already says `partial`, so this omission does not change the system union or imply absence. Withhold a complete comparison of which retained inputs have learning authority across update consumers; the output's knowledge/instruction classifications and the positive trace-learning finding remain supported.\n",
      "id": "000027-apply-profile-verification-1",
